// case: for-over-never-set-dynamic-field
// what: a `for` lowers to list_len/list_get with no runtime kind check, so
//      iterating a dynamic field that was never set miscompiles: the read
//      answers "" (get_raw) and the loop walks it as a list. Measured today:
//      `.len()` prints garbage (774176871), iteration segfaults
//      (exit -1073741819, no output), print shows a pointer. A check-time
//      guard was tried and reverted: it rejected three green suite tests
//      iterating DECLARED list fields (model_literal_fields,
//      generic_nested_argument, generic_models), whose reads also type
//      "unknown" because checkNode never consults model field declarations.
//      The sound fix needs model-field typing with generic substitution, not
//      a broader guard. FINDINGS F-0024.
//
//      Repro (do not run blindly -- it crashes the process):
//        val o = { name: "x" }
//        for t in o.tags { print(t) }
// expect-error: for loops iterate lists
fn main() -> int {
    val o = { name: "x" }
    for t in o.tags {
        print(t)
    }
    return 0
}
